<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Soutpansberg</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Zoutpansberg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Soutpansberg is a mountain range in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limpopo">Limpopo</a> province in the far north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>, named after a salt pan at its western end. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andries-hendrik-potgieter">Andries Hendrik Potgieter</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/voortrekkers">Voortrekkers</a> settled at its foot in 1848, founding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schoemansdal">Schoemansdal</a>, the centre of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> republic later absorbed into the South African Republic. The region is home to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venda-people">Venda people</a> and is rich in plant and animal life.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/soutpansberg.jpg" alt="Soutpansberg" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Petrus Potgieter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vivo_Limpopo_SouthAfrica_June2009.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
